# Cloudflare build output and local state.
#
# Not merely noise. `@opennextjs/cloudflare` inlines the resolved environment into
# `.open-next/cloudflare/next-env.mjs`, and with a Neon-linked `.env.local` that file contains a live
# `DATABASE_URL` — password and all. The directory was untracked but not ignored, so 34 files were
# stageable and `git add -A` would have committed a production database credential.
#
# The secret scanner caught it, which is the only reason this is a note rather than an incident.
.open-next/
.wrangler/

# Agent skills and local agent settings.
#
# `.claude/skills/` holds 148 vendored third-party skills (Google Cloud, Three.js, Neon) totalling
# ~6 MB across 724 files. They are development tooling: nothing in the build, the tests or CI reads
# them, and vendoring Apache-2.0 content into a private product repo adds licence-tracking burden for
# no build benefit. Reproduce them from `E:\Project\skills-src` (see docs/DEVELOPMENT_STORY.md).
#
# `settings.local.json` is per-machine by definition — the name says so.
.claude/skills/
.claude/settings.local.json
